{"title":"Career Roadmap · Play Researcher","role":"Play Researcher","summary":"A Play Researcher studies how children, teenagers, adults, families, and different user groups play, learn, interact, explore, compete, collaborate, and experience games and toys. The role combines design research, psychology, observation, usability testing, play theory, product development, and human behaviour.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Toy & Game Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Play Researcher may work on toys, board games, educational products, digital games, playgrounds, learning experiences, children's media, and emerging interactive products."},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Toy & Game Design","Design Research / Playtesting Intern","Junior Play Researcher","Play Researcher","Senior Play Researcher / Play Research Lead","Research & Design Strategy"],"label":"Typical route"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Play research can be applied across:"},{"type":"table","header":["Area","Opportunities"],"rows":[[{"text":"Toy Industry"},{"text":"Toy research, playtesting, product research"}],[{"text":"Board Games"},{"text":"Game mechanics and player research"}],[{"text":"Digital Games"},{"text":"Player research and usability"}],[{"text":"Educational Products"},{"text":"Learning-through-play research"}],[{"text":"Children's Products"},{"text":"Child-centred product development"}],[{"text":"EdTech"},{"text":"Gamification and learning experiences"}],[{"text":"Playgrounds"},{"text":"Play-space research"}],[{"text":"Museums"},{"text":"Interactive learning experiences"}],[{"text":"Children's Media"},{"text":"Audience and interaction research"}],[{"text":"UX Research"},{"text":"User research and usability testing"}],[{"text":"Consumer Research"},{"text":"Behaviour and preference research"}],[{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Inclusive play research"}],[{"text":"Game Studios"},{"text":"Player experience research"}],[{"text":"Design Consultancies"},{"text":"Research-led product strategy"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year-by-Year Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Foundations of Play & Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Build an understanding of design, observation and human behaviour."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design fundamentals"},{"text":"Observation techniques"},{"text":"Basic psychology"},{"text":"Child development fundamentals"},{"text":"Introduction to play theory"},{"text":"Creativity and ideation"},{"text":"Visual communication"},{"text":"Storytelling"},{"text":"Sketching"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Research documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What is play?"},{"text":"Why do people play?"},{"text":"Different types of play"},{"text":"Individual vs social play"},{"text":"Structured vs unstructured play"},{"text":"Competitive vs cooperative play"},{"text":"Physical vs digital play"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Projects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Observe how children interact with an existing toy"},{"text":"Compare three board games"},{"text":"Document different types of play"},{"text":"Design a simple physical play activity"},{"text":"Conduct a small play-observation study"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Play Research & User Studies"},{"type":"p","text":"Move from observation to structured research."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User research"},{"text":"Interviews"},{"text":"Contextual inquiry"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Focus groups"},{"text":"Playtesting"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Behaviour mapping"},{"text":"Affinity mapping"},{"text":"Research synthesis"},{"text":"Persona development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Study"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Child behaviour"},{"text":"Cognitive development"},{"text":"Social interaction"},{"text":"Motivation"},{"text":"Attention"},{"text":"Creativity"},{"text":"Learning"},{"text":"Collaboration"},{"text":"Competition"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Miro"},{"text":"FigJam"},{"text":"Notion"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Google Forms"},{"text":"Adobe Creative Cloud"},{"text":"Basic statistical tools"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Professional Play Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop professional research capability."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Experimental design"},{"text":"Research ethics"},{"text":"Research protocols"},{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Behavioural analysis"},{"text":"Player journey mapping"},{"text":"Game usability"},{"text":"Play pattern analysis"},{"text":"Product evaluation"},{"text":"A/B testing fundamentals"},{"text":"Research reporting"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced research questions"},{"type":"p","text":"Instead of asking:"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Do children like this toy?\""},{"type":"p","text":"Investigate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What behaviour does the toy encourage?"},{"text":"How long does engagement last?"},{"text":"Where does the child lose interest?"},{"text":"What causes repeated play?"},{"text":"Does the toy encourage exploration?"},{"text":"Does it support social interaction?"},{"text":"Is the difficulty appropriate?"},{"text":"Can different abilities use it?"},{"text":"Does the product encourage creativity?"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This shift from opinion collection to behavioural evidence is a major professional skill."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Specialisation & Industry Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose a research direction."},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation A — Children's Play"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Developmental stages"},{"text":"Cognitive play"},{"text":"Social play"},{"text":"Imaginative play"},{"text":"Motor skills"},{"text":"Educational play"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation B — Game Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Player motivation"},{"text":"Game mechanics"},{"text":"Engagement"},{"text":"Difficulty"},{"text":"Retention"},{"text":"Player behaviour"},{"text":"UX"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation C — Educational Play"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Learning outcomes"},{"text":"Gamification"},{"text":"STEM toys"},{"text":"Learning activities"},{"text":"Educational games"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation D — Inclusive Play"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Accessible toys"},{"text":"Universal design"},{"text":"Assistive play"},{"text":"Neurodiverse users"},{"text":"Physical accessibility"},{"text":"Inclusive game mechanics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialisation E — Play Spaces"},{"type":"p","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Playground behaviour"},{"text":"Spatial interaction"},{"text":"Social play"},{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Environmental design"},{"text":"Public play spaces"}]}]},{"heading":"Internship Roadmap","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design research internships"},{"text":"Educational product internships"},{"text":"Children's activity organizations"},{"text":"Museum education programs"},{"text":"Toy design studios"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Toy companies"},{"text":"Board-game companies"},{"text":"EdTech companies"},{"text":"Game studios"},{"text":"Children's product companies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3–4"},{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Consumer research teams"},{"text":"UX research teams"},{"text":"Game research teams"},{"text":"Toy R&D teams"},{"text":"Educational product research"},{"text":"Design consultancies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful internship titles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design Research Intern"},{"text":"Playtesting Intern"},{"text":"UX Research Intern"},{"text":"Game Research Intern"},{"text":"Toy Design Intern"},{"text":"Consumer Research Intern"},{"text":"User Research Intern"},{"text":"Product Research Intern"}]}]},{"heading":"Strong Internship Project","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"\"How Children Play With Educational Toys\""},{"type":"p","text":"Conduct a complete research study."},{"type":"h","text":"Step 1 — Research Question"},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"p","text":"How does physical interaction influence engagement with STEM learning toys?"},{"type":"h","text":"Step 2 — Observation"},{"type":"p","text":"Observe:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interaction time"},{"text":"Repeated actions"},{"text":"Frustration"},{"text":"Collaboration"},{"text":"Exploration"},{"text":"Problem-solving"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Step 3 — Interviews"},{"type":"p","text":"Talk to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Children where ethically and appropriately permitted"},{"text":"Parents"},{"text":"Teachers"},{"text":"Facilitators"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Step 4 — Analyse"},{"type":"p","text":"Identify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Behaviour patterns"},{"text":"Pain points"},{"text":"Engagement triggers"},{"text":"Learning opportunities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Step 5 — Prototype"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop an improved toy concept."},{"type":"h","text":"Step 6 — Playtest"},{"type":"p","text":"Compare the original and improved versions."},{"type":"h","text":"Step 7 — Report"},{"type":"p","text":"Present:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Research","Evidence","Insight","Design Opportunity","Prototype","Testing","Recommendations"]},{"type":"p","text":"This is an excellent portfolio case study."}]},{"heading":"Research Ethics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Because Play Researchers may work with children, ethical practice is essential."},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Informed consent"},{"text":"Parent/guardian consent where required"},{"text":"Child assent"},{"text":"Privacy"},{"text":"Data protection"},{"text":"Safe observation"},{"text":"Non-invasive research"},{"text":"Appropriate recording practices"},{"text":"Institutional research procedures"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Never treat children simply as \"test users.\" Their safety, dignity and comfort must be prioritised."}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UX Research"},{"text":"Design Research"},{"text":"User-Centred Design"},{"text":"Human-Centred Design"},{"text":"Child development fundamentals"},{"text":"Game design"},{"text":"Play theory"},{"text":"Educational psychology fundamentals"},{"text":"Qualitative research"},{"text":"Quantitative research"},{"text":"Usability testing"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Data visualization"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful tools:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Miro/FigJam"},{"text":"Notion"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"SPSS or equivalent statistical tools"},{"text":"R/Python for advanced research analysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Certificates should support practical research capability rather than replace actual studies."}]},{"heading":"Careers You Can Be Hired As","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Possible entry-level roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Play Research Intern"},{"text":"Junior Play Researcher"},{"text":"Design Researcher"},{"text":"UX Researcher"},{"text":"User Research Assistant"},{"text":"Game Research Assistant"},{"text":"Consumer Research Assistant"},{"text":"Toy Research Assistant"},{"text":"Product Researcher"},{"text":"Educational Product Researcher"},{"text":"Game UX Researcher"},{"text":"Research Coordinator"}]},{"type":"p","text":"With experience:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Senior Play Researcher"},{"text":"Senior UX Researcher"},{"text":"Player Researcher"},{"text":"Research Lead"},{"text":"Play Research Lead"},{"text":"Consumer Insights Manager"},{"text":"Research Strategist"},{"text":"Design Research Manager"}]}]},{"heading":"Interview Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Research Questions"},{"type":"p","text":"Be prepared to explain:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What is play research?"},{"text":"How would you study children's play?"},{"text":"How do you conduct a playtest?"},{"text":"Difference between qualitative and quantitative research"},{"text":"What is contextual inquiry?"},{"text":"How do you reduce researcher bias?"},{"text":"How do you analyse observational data?"},{"text":"How do you identify behavioural patterns?"},{"text":"How do you measure engagement?"},{"text":"What makes a good research question?"},{"text":"How would you test a new toy?"},{"text":"How do you convert research findings into design recommendations?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Case Study Challenge"},{"type":"p","text":"You might receive:"},{"type":"p","text":"\"Children stop using a learning toy after five minutes. Find out why.\""},{"type":"p","text":"A strong approach:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Observe","Interview","Analyse behaviour","Identify friction","Form hypotheses","Prototype","Playtest","Measure","Recommend"]}]},{"heading":"Portfolio Structure","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Play Research portfolio should demonstrate research thinking, not simply attractive toy designs."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Play Observation"},{"type":"p","text":"Show:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Research question"},{"text":"Participants/context"},{"text":"Observation framework"},{"text":"Behaviour map"},{"text":"Findings"},{"text":"Insights"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Toy Playtest"},{"type":"p","text":"Show:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Prototype"},{"text":"Test methodology"},{"text":"Observations"},{"text":"User feedback"},{"text":"Iterations"},{"text":"Final recommendations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Board Game Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Analyse:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mechanics"},{"text":"Player behaviour"},{"text":"Difficulty"},{"text":"Engagement"},{"text":"Social interaction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Educational Play"},{"type":"p","text":"Study whether a play experience actually supports the intended learning outcome."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Inclusive Play"},{"type":"p","text":"Research how a toy/game could be adapted for users with different physical, sensory or cognitive needs."}]},{"heading":"High-Value Specialist Routes","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Route A — Toy Industry Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Toy Research Intern","Play Researcher","Senior Play Researcher","R&D Research Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"Best for physical toys and children's products."},{"type":"h","text":"Route B — Game / Player Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Game UX","Playtesting","Player Researcher","Senior Player Researcher","Research Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Player behaviour"},{"text":"UX"},{"text":"Game mechanics"},{"text":"Engagement"},{"text":"Difficulty"},{"text":"Retention"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Route C — Educational Play"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Educational Product Research","Learning Through Play","Learning Experience Researcher"]},{"type":"p","text":"Combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Design","Play","Learning","Behaviour"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Route D — UX Research"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Design Research","UX Research","Senior UX Researcher","Research Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"This is one of the most transferable career routes."},{"type":"h","text":"Route E — Inclusive Play"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Accessibility Research","Inclusive Toy/Game Research","Inclusive Design Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"Strong long-term potential as accessibility and universal design become increasingly important."}]},{"heading":"Play Research Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A professional project can follow:"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Question"},{"type":"h","text":"Background Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Research Protocol"},{"type":"h","text":"Recruitment"},{"type":"h","text":"Observation / Interviews"},{"type":"h","text":"Playtesting"},{"type":"h","text":"Data Collection"},{"type":"h","text":"Qualitative / Quantitative Analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Behavioural Insights"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Opportunities"},{"type":"h","text":"Prototype"},{"type":"h","text":"Second Playtest"},{"type":"h","text":"Recommendations"},{"type":"p","text":"This demonstrates that research is not simply \"asking users what they like.\""}]},{"heading":"Portfolio Projects to Build Before Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Project","Main Skill"],"rows":[[{"text":"Educational Toy Playtest"},{"text":"Child-centred research"}],[{"text":"Board Game Behaviour Study"},{"text":"Game research"}],[{"text":"Playground Observation"},{"text":"Environmental play"}],[{"text":"STEM Toy Evaluation"},{"text":"Learning through play"}],[{"text":"Mobile Game UX Study"},{"text":"Digital player research"}],[{"text":"Inclusive Toy Study"},{"text":"Accessibility"}],[{"text":"Family Game Research"},{"text":"Social play"}],[{"text":"Toy Usability Study"},{"text":"Usability testing"}],[{"text":"Gamification Research"},{"text":"Behaviour & motivation"}],[{"text":"Future Play Study"},{"text":"Emerging technology"}]]}]},{"heading":"AI and Future of Play Research","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI will increasingly help researchers with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Interview transcription"},{"text":"Qualitative coding"},{"text":"Behaviour classification"},{"text":"Pattern detection"},{"text":"Survey analysis"},{"text":"Research synthesis"},{"text":"Player segmentation"},{"text":"Personalised game experiences"},{"text":"Adaptive difficulty analysis"},{"text":"Generative game prototyping"},{"text":"Predictive player analytics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"However, AI cannot completely replace contextual observation and human interpretation."},{"type":"p","text":"A strong future Play Researcher should combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Human Behaviour","Play Theory","Research Methods","Data Analysis","AI-Assisted Research"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Emerging Research Areas","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Students should explore:"},{"type":"h","text":"AI & Play"},{"type":"p","text":"How generative AI changes children's creativity and play."},{"type":"h","text":"AI Toys"},{"type":"p","text":"How conversational and adaptive toys affect interaction."},{"type":"h","text":"Screen-Free Digital-Physical Play"},{"type":"p","text":"Combining physical toys with digital experiences."},{"type":"h","text":"XR Play"},{"type":"p","text":"AR/VR-based play experiences."},{"type":"h","text":"Adaptive Games"},{"type":"p","text":"Games that change difficulty based on player behaviour."},{"type":"h","text":"Inclusive Play"},{"type":"p","text":"Designing experiences for diverse abilities."},{"type":"h","text":"Sustainable Play"},{"type":"p","text":"Long-life, repairable and recyclable toys."},{"type":"h","text":"Social Play"},{"type":"p","text":"Understanding collaboration, communication and competition."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad Options","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Relevant postgraduate areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design Research"},{"text":"Interaction Design"},{"text":"UX Research"},{"text":"Game Design"},{"text":"Game Studies"},{"text":"Child-Centred Design"},{"text":"Educational Design"},{"text":"Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"Design Psychology"},{"text":"Learning Sciences"},{"text":"Play & Creativity Studies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Potential destinations include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"USA"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Sweden"},{"text":"Denmark"},{"text":"Finland"},{"text":"Australia"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, prioritise programs offering research labs, user studies, child-centred design, game research, HCI, psychology or learning-science collaborations."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Pathways","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Research-Oriented"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Des Design Research"},{"text":"MA Design Research"},{"text":"MSc Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"MSc User Experience"},{"text":"MA Interaction Design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Game-Oriented"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MA Game Design"},{"text":"MSc Game Technology"},{"text":"Game Studies"},{"text":"Player Experience Research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Education-Oriented"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Learning Sciences"},{"text":"Educational Technology"},{"text":"Educational Psychology"},{"text":"Learning Experience Design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"p","text":"A PhD can be appropriate for careers in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Academic research"},{"text":"Child development research"},{"text":"Play research"},{"text":"Game studies"},{"text":"HCI"},{"text":"Learning sciences"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"0–2 Years"},{"type":"p","text":"Research Assistant / Junior Play Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"2–5 Years"},{"type":"p","text":"Play Researcher / UX Researcher / Player Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"5–8 Years"},{"type":"p","text":"Senior Researcher / Research Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"8–12 Years"},{"type":"p","text":"Research Lead / Play Research Lead / UX Research Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"12+ Years"},{"type":"p","text":"Research Director / Head of Research / Design Strategy Director"}]},{"heading":"2040–2046 Career Evolution","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The Play Researcher of the future may work on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI companions"},{"text":"Adaptive toys"},{"text":"AI-powered games"},{"text":"Mixed-reality play"},{"text":"Robotics and play"},{"text":"Digital twins of play environments"},{"text":"Personalised learning games"},{"text":"Generative game worlds"},{"text":"Neuroadaptive interfaces"},{"text":"Inclusive adaptive play"},{"text":"Human-AI interaction through play"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The profession may evolve from simply studying how people play toward designing and evaluating adaptive human-AI play ecosystems."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User interviews"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"Ethnography"},{"text":"Surveys"},{"text":"Focus groups"},{"text":"Playtesting"},{"text":"Usability testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Behaviour"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Child development"},{"text":"Cognitive psychology fundamentals"},{"text":"Motivation"},{"text":"Social interaction"},{"text":"Learning"},{"text":"Behavioural analysis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Play"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Play theory"},{"text":"Game mechanics"},{"text":"Player experience"},{"text":"Game usability"},{"text":"Educational play"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Analysis"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Qualitative coding"},{"text":"Research synthesis"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Data visualization"},{"text":"Behaviour mapping"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Game design"},{"text":"Toy design"},{"text":"Interaction design"},{"text":"Service design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Figma"},{"text":"Miro/FigJam"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Basic Python/R"},{"text":"AI research tools"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["Design foundations","observation","play theory"],"sep":"+","label":"Year 1"},{"type":"flow","items":["User research","playtesting","behavioural research"],"sep":"+","label":"Year 2"},{"type":"flow","items":["Advanced research","analysis","prototyping"],"sep":"+","label":"Year 3"},{"type":"flow","items":["Specialisation","industry research","major portfolio study"],"sep":"+","label":"Year 4"},{"type":"note","label":"Graduation","text":"Junior Play Researcher / Design Researcher / UX Researcher"},{"type":"note","label":"3–5 Years","text":"Play Researcher / Player Researcher / UX Researcher"},{"type":"note","label":"5–10 Years","text":"Senior Researcher / Research Lead"},{"type":"note","label":"10+ Years","text":"Research Director / Head of Research / Design Strategy Lead"}]},{"heading":"Best Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong B.Des Toy & Game Design graduate targeting Play Research should graduate with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Strong understanding of play theory"},{"text":"Child-centred research skills"},{"text":"User observation skills"},{"text":"Playtesting experience"},{"text":"Interview and survey skills"},{"text":"Qualitative research capability"},{"text":"Basic quantitative analysis"},{"text":"Game mechanics knowledge"},{"text":"Toy prototyping skills"},{"text":"UX research fundamentals"},{"text":"Research ethics awareness"},{"text":"At least 4–6 substantial research case studies"},{"text":"Experience working with real users"},{"text":"One complete toy playtest"},{"text":"One game/player research project"},{"text":"One educational-play study"},{"text":"One inclusive-play study"},{"text":"Strong research documentation"},{"text":"Professional portfolio"},{"text":"AI-assisted research literacy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Ideal final skill stack"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Toy & Game Design","Play Theory","Child-Centred Research","User Research","Playtesting","Game/ Toy Prototyping","Behavioural Analysis","UX Research","Qualitative & Quantitative Methods","Data Visualization","Accessibility","AI-Assisted Research","Professional Research Portfolio"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This combination prepares the graduate for roles across toy companies, game studios, EdTech, UX research, children's products, educational design, museums, play-space design, consumer research and emerging AI-powered play experiences."}]}]}